\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee at record low, rupiah falls to Aug 1998 trough\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2008\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah fell to its lowest levels since the Asian financial crisis and the Indian rupee hit a record low on Thursday, driven by investors' growing fears of a global recession and capital flight from those countries.\par \par \uc2  At the same time, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to pump funds into the market to stop its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaching the upper limit of its 7.75-7.85 band against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  Investors exiting carry trades and risky markets have been pumping money into the safety of the pegged Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah <IDR=> hit 12,400 per dollar, an August 1998 trough, in trading marked by illiquidity and verbal and dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "BI is not happy whenever we buy dollars. They are making calls almost every single hour asking us about our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions," one trader at a foreign bank in Jakarta said, declining to be identified. "That's why there are few deals done."\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen 16.5 percent against the dollar in the last three weeks, pressured by worries over the huge foreign holdings of its debt market and corporates' ability to service their large overseas borrowings.\par \par \uc2  Asian stock markets fell sharply on Thursday, with investors' even gloomier about global growth after the U.S. Federal Reserve warned of protracted weakness in the economy and hopes for a bailout for the troubled U.S. automakers dimmed.\par \par \uc2  "The market is still in risk reduction mode apparently," said Han-Sia Yeo, a strategist at Bank Of America\par \par \uc2  "But the (dollar) buying pressure is not as intense as in October or May periods. The worst period is probably over, but liquidity will be quite bad for the balance of the year."\par \par \uc2  "It's going to difficult to expect investors to put on risk in a significant manner ahead of year end," he said.\par \par \uc2  The rupee <INR=IN> fell to a record low of 50.6 per dollar, after which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of selling dollars through state-run banks.\par \par \uc2  The Korean won <KRW=> fell 3.4 percent, closing at its weakest in nearly 11 years. [nSEO339969]. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0716 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.22          95.90       +0.71\par  Sing dlr        1.5295         1.5290       -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      33.420         33.265       -0.46\par  Korean won     1496.00        1446.50       -3.31\par  Baht             35.10          35.00       -0.28\par  Peso             49.88          49.89       +0.02\par  Rupiah        12150.00       11850.00       -2.47\par  Rupee            50.51          49.99       -1.02\par  Ringgit         3.6220         3.6080       -0.39\par  Yuan            6.8340         6.8285       -0.08\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.22         111.33      +16.92\par  Sing dlr        1.5295         1.4382       -5.97\par  Taiwan dlr      33.420         32.443       -2.92\par  Korean won     1496.00         935.7