\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia cbank: won't allow 'irrational' rupiah level\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2008\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not let the rupiah <IDR=> hit "irrational" levels, Bank Indonesia's governor said on Tuesday, following a further depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Boediono's comments came after the rupiah hit a fresh 7-year low against the dollar on Tuesday, once again at the fore of declines in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred by falling stock markets and increasing evidence pointing to a global recession.\par \par \uc2 "We will steer it towards a good and realistic level. We will not let the market make our exchange rate irrational," Boediono said. He did not elaborate further.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah briefly fell 2.9 percent to 12,050 to the dollar, with some dealers expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken towards 12,100 in the coming week due to market worries over foreign fund outflows from the country's financial market.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia imports a significant amount of basic necessities especially food. Failure to stabilise the rupiah, which has fallen 21 percent this year, could push up the cost of imported foods and put pressure on the country's balance of payments.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to defend its falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it has also introduced a new measure on buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For more details on the new ruling please double click on [ID:nJAK67958] and [ID:nJAK426305].\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark interest rate <BIPG> unchanged at 9.5 percent, also to underpin the rupiah, even though it has kept the cost of borrowing relatively high.\par \par \uc2 But with growth risks likely to increase as the world downturn deepens, rate cuts are a matter of time, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Southeast Asia's biggest economy expanded 6.11 percent in the third quarter, its weakest pace in more than a year, reflecting a slide in commodities prices as global demand deteriorates. (Writing by Tyagita Silka; Editing by Sugita Katyal)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL-INDONESIA/RUPIAH (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|IF|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081118e4bi000hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
