\par\par \b \uc2 Reuters Southeast Asia News Highlights 0900 GMT Oct 27\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid against the dollar as investors dumped assets amid heightened fears of a global downturn, forcing central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Philippines to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> bore the brunt of the selling, briefly hitting a low of 10,800 per dollar but later steadying near 10,600 thanks to official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - Thailand, the world's biggest rice exporter, plans to barter rice for oil from Iran, its commerce minister said.\par \par \uc2 "Our senior officials plan to go to Iran by the middle of November to discuss the specifications of oil and rice that would be exchanged," Commerce Minister Chaiya Sasomsab told reporters.\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 MANILA - Philippine shares plummeted a record 12.3 percent as investors continued to dump emerging market equities due to worries of a sharp global downturn, which also battered other Asian markets.\par \par \uc2 "There's no other word for it but a bloodbath," said Alejandro Yu, president at RS Lim and Co. "There was a massive selldown across the board."\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 HANOI - The Vietnamese dong may fall to 17,000 per dollar soon due to strong demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from importers and equity investors, bankers said.\par \par \uc2 "The rise in the dollar against the dong is not abnormal and is not synonymous with a deep depreciation in the dong," Doan Huu Tue, of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking development strategy department, was quoted as saying in a government monetary market report.\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - Thailand, the world's biggest rubber producer, plans to cut production by 700,000 tonnes in the six months starting from October to shore up prices, the Agriculture Ministry said.\par \par \uc2 "We will encourage farmers to tap less latex as we aim to cut rubber supply by 50 percent between October to March," Deputy Agriculture Minister Theerachai Saenkaew, who oversees rubber matters, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 - - - - (Compiled by Carl Bagh)\par \par \uc2 SOUTHEAST ASIA-HIGHLIGHTS 0900 GMT|LANGEN|Table|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA|G|RBN|SI|IF|PHD|RNP|DNP|PGE|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar000wi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
