\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia unveils more crisis measures, IMF positive\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ed Davies and Adriana Nina Kusuma   \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2008\par 13:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Indonesia is well placed to weather a global economic crisis, an IMF official said on Wednesday, as Southeast Asia's top economy unveiled more measures to shore up confidence in its capital and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Investor confidence took a dive last week and stocks in Jakarta plunged, prompting the closure of the stock exchange for three days and pressing policy-makers to quickly push through several measures in order to avoid a replay of the crisis that battered Indonesia's economy a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> and the stock market <.JKSE>, which reopened on Monday, have been more stable this week, alongside a global rebound in market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals are very strong and it's in good shape to weather this turmoil," said Milan Zavadjil, the International Monetary Fund's senior representative in Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 The IMF led a $43 billion rescue package for Indonesia a decade ago after it was hit by the Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 He said that growth in Indonesia was much more reliant on domestic consumption and it was not as exposed to potential slowdowns in exports to markets such as the United States and Europe, in contrast to Singapore and the Philippines.\par \par \uc2 "Consumption currently has a lot of momentum and it's not suddenly going to stop dead," he told a panel discussion on the global crisis, adding that Indonesia's "fiscal position is sound" and that it had relatively low government debt levels.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's economy grew 6.3 percent last year, the fastest pace in over a decade, aided by exports of commodities including palm oil, rubber, gas, and a steady drop in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Analysts, however, expect global demand for key exports of commodities and mining products to be hit by the credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 GUARANTEES\par \par \uc2 Zavadjil said that while Indonesia was exposed to a drop in commodity prices, export volumes were unlikely to fall, noting that a lot of exports go to China where growth should hold up better.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's parliamentary budget commission on Wednesday approved an economic growth forecast of 6 percent for 2009.\par \par \uc2 Along with the authorities halting stock trading last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the rupiah, particularly when it neared 10,000/dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia moved on Monday to raise its guarantees on bank deposits to 2 billion rupiah ($203,000), up from 100 million rupiah previously, following similar steps taken by governments across the world that were aimed at tackling the biggest financial crisis since the Great Depression.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's maximum guaranteed rupiah deposit rates were rasied this week by 75 basis points to 10 percent, part of efforts to bolster confidence in the rupiah and after a sharp increase in the amount of deposits it guarantees. Firdaus Djaelani, the head of state-owned deposit insurance corporation LPS said in a telephone text message late on Tuesday night that the agency had kept its guaranteed dollar deposit rates unchanged at 3.5 percent. Both were effective Oct. 14. As in other economies, Indonesian's interbank money market had been hit by the global credit crisis. But unlike some others, the liquidity squeeze in the domestic money market had also been made worse due to lower deposit growth relative to loan growth.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesia Stock Exchange may also increase the upside limit for share trading to 20-25 percent from 10 percent currently, President Director Erry Firmansyah said on Wednesday, but will keep its 10 percent downside limit in place. (Additional reporting by Andreas Ismar; Editing by Sara Webb)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/INDONESIA|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|O|OIL|IF|SI|ABX|G|RNP|DNP|PGE|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081015e4af0013l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
