\par\par \b \uc2 USD Ends At IDR9,935; Dollar Off Intraday High Of IDR10,000\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 11:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah weakened sharply against the dollar Friday, falling amid thin trade to close at its weakest since December 2005.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded at IDR9,935 at the close of local trading after hitting an intraday high of IDR10,000. The dollar had closed Thursday at IDR9,655.\par \par \uc2 It was the weakest level for the rupiah since Dec. 2, 2005, when the dollar fetched IDR9,990.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rupiah weakened due to panic-buying of dollars as a safe haven amid the current uncertainty over local stocks.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesia Stock Exchange remained closed Friday, its third day of suspension after a trading halt was declared halfway through the morning session Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said that had the bourse opened as planned for Friday's afternoon trading session, both the rupiah and domestic stocks would probably have fallen more.\par \par \uc2 The exchange's composite index fell more than 21% this week prior to the trading halt. A 25-basis-point hike in the Bank Indonesia policy rate Tuesday also hurt growth expectations and increased bearishness on the bourse.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said that dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forward contracts rose sharply. The one-week offshore NDFs reached IDR10,025in early trading Friday, they said, compared with IDR9,950.\par \par \uc2 The spot market weakened more slowly, probably due to heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold as much as $400 million Friday and around $2.5 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so far this week, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot see (the market fundamentals) too clearly as (today) the market has been very thin," a dealer at a major foreign bank said. "It seemed to take (the dollar) no effort to get from IDR9,900 to IDR10,000" as liquidity was so tight.\par \par \uc2 The dollar may rise more Monday when the stock market re-opens. Dealers said, however, that the weekend break will likely prompt investors to re-assess fundamentals, which might mean that shares likely won't tank further.\par \par \uc2 They said the dollar should find resistance at IDR10,000 and be supported at IDR9,850.\par \par \uc2 -By Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 10-10-08 0947GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081010e4aa000hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
