\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank deputy says "no liquidity problem"\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2008\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 17 (Reuters) - An Indonesian deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday "there is no liquidity problem" in the banking sector, a day after Bank Indonesia reduced its overnight repo rate to help commercial banks cope with a liquidity squeeze.\par \par \uc2 Even before the latest wave of credit turmoil struck global markets, Indonesian money market had been squeezed by foreign investors' selling local bonds and gradual policy tightening by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its battle to contain double-digit inflation.\par \par \uc2 Rapid growth in loans in step with a still fast expanding Indonesian economy, outstripping growth in bank deposits, also contributed to the tight liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "In regards to liquidity conditions in the banking sector, there is no problem," deputy governor Budi Rochadi told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "Of course liquidity is an important issue to meet needs (for cash) for the Eid al-Fitr celebrations," Rochadi said, adding that "in regards to liquidity, we will make it easier for banks to meet their liquidity needs including through repo."\par \par \uc2 Rochadi was referring to the Eid celebration to mark the end of the Muslim fasting month of Ramadan, which this year falls in early October. Demand for cash usually rises ahead of the celebrations as families head to their home towns to visit relatives.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday cut its overnight repo rate, the rate at which it lends to commercial banks, by 200 basis point to 10.25 percent and raised the rate it pays on overnight deposits -- also known as the Fasbi rate -- by 100 basis points to 8.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia also offered to pay more on deposits that banks place with it, offering local lenders extra help at a time when markets have been rattled by the collapse of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , the takeover of crisis-hit \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  and funding troubles at insurer \uc2 American International Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Separately, another deputy governor, Hartadi Sarwono, said on Wednesday that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars to support the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <IDR=>, in recent days.\par \par \uc2 He also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering revising its reserve requirement ruling for commercial banks under which the requirement would no longer be linked to banks' loan ratios but to the possible use of debt paper by commercial banks in meeting the requirement.\par \par \uc2 "It is no longer relevant for the current minimum reserve requirements to be linked to the LDR (loan to deposit ratios)," Sarwono told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "Now the (annual) loan growth is over 35 percent, so we will try to revoke this ruling. There is possibility the minimum reserve requirements will no longer be related with LDR but with debt paper."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tyagita Silka; Writing by Gde Anugrah Arka; Editing by Ed Davies)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/C.BANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080917e49h000ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
