\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Bk Indonesia:To Maintain Continual Presence In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2008\par 08:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor; vice president's comment)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia maintains a constant presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will respond to any market moves driven by fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Boediono told reporters Friday.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoids responding to market movements it deems temporary, and measures its responses to avoid excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Boediono told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Also Friday, Vice President Jusuf Kalla told reporters that the possibility of the dollar reaching IDR9,500 is "not a concern."\par \par \uc2 "We can still overcome (that level of rupiah weakness)," Kalla said. "It will of course cause losses for importers, but on the other hand, it benefits exporters, so it isn't a problem. This is a temporary up-and-down move."\par \par \uc2 Boediono said the authorities "must respond to all movements of the markets that have fundamental characteristics, but not to those that are temporary."\par \par \uc2 "We must be on guard (to ensure) our response does not have a 'rhythm' that is excessive, whether it is in (the form of changes to) interest rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 " \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Boediono made the remarks after the dollar strengthened to around IDR9,460, its highest level since Jan. 23, when it reached IDR9,475 in intraday trading.\par \par \uc2 He didn't say whether he thought the rupiah's weakness Friday was driven by fundamentals, but reiterated official remarks earlier this week that Indonesia's economic fundamentals are sound.\par \par \uc2 "Our fundamentals are fine and I am very certain that we can calmly overcome" the weakening in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and overall weakening in world financial markets. "All countries now must align their (policies) with the changes that have taken place in the global market."\par \par \uc2 Boediono didn't say whether Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday.\par \par \uc2 Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold several hundred million dollars in recent days to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna, contributing to Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 12-09-08 0654GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080912e49c0008g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
