\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia raises rph deposit rate, holds dlr rate\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2008\par 10:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 11 (Reuters) - Indonesia's deposit insurance agency said it would raise its guaranteed rupiah deposit rate with effect from Monday, but analysts said the new rate was lower than expected, and failed to provide support for the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> fell more than 1 percent to 9,475 per dollar on Thursday, its weakest since late January, as troubles in the U.S. financial sector reduced appetite for riskier assets. Traders said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Firdaus Djaelani, head of the state-owned deposit insurance corporation (known as LPS), said the agency had raised its rupiah guaranteed bank deposit rate by 50 basis points to 9.25 percent for the period Sept. 15, 2008 to Jan. 14, 2009.\par \par \uc2 The agency kept the maximum dollar guaranteed bank deposit rate at 3.50 percent. Analysts said that would make it less attractive for holders of rupiah to switch into dollars, a move aimed at reducing selling pressure on the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The maximum guaranteed bank deposit rates are usually closely watched by commercial banks because they affect the commercial banks' deposit and lending rates, and therefore affect their profitability.\par \par \uc2 "We're anticipating inflationary pressure...many have predicted inflation will remain in double digits until year-end, so we're anticipating that," Djaelani told Reuters by telephone when asked about the reasons behind the deposit rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's inflation rate inched lower to 11.85 percent in August on the back of lower oil prices, but food prices and transportation fees typically rise during the Muslim fasting month of Ramadan, which this year started on September 1.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia forecast inflation at 11.5-12.5 percent this year before easing to 6.5-7.5 percent at the end of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark interest rate, known as the BI rate <BIPG>, by 25 basis points to 9.25 percent last week, the fifth time this year, to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts had expected the deposit agency to raise the maximum deposit rates by more than 50 basis points in order to encourage investors to park their funds in rupiah.\par \par \uc2 "In my view (the hike) should have been bigger," said Anton Gunawan, economist at Bank Danamon.\par \par \uc2 Some commercial banks now offer deposit rates of around 12 percent, much higher than the guaranteed rates, as banks are competing for depositors' funds amid tight market liquidity following monetary tightening by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Andreas Ismar and Adriana Nina Kusuma, writing by Tyagita Silka, editing by Sara Webb)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-RATES/DEPOSIT (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|IF|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080911e49b000ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
