\par\par \b \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS-Indonesian c.bank gov comments on rupiah fall\b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2008\par 09:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Following are comments by Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Boediono about the rupiah fall, made to reporters on Friday.\par \par \uc2  For related story, please click story [ID:nJKB000823]\par \par \uc2  ON RUPIAH FALL\par \par \uc2  "This is a global tendency, the dollar has been strengthening against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world."\par \par \uc2  "This is just market swings."\par \par \uc2  WILL THE RUPIAH STRENGTHEN ?\par \par \uc2  "I think if we look at the fundamentals, I suppose it would be fair if (the rupiah) is at levels that are in line with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region."\par \par \uc2  NO SPECIFIC TARGET\par \par \uc2  "We are of course monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements including in the region. We, of course, cannot go against the flow, we will not target any specific levels."\par \par \uc2  MARKET \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "always in the market."\par \par \uc2  "No. We will be in the market to reduce the volatility," he said when asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is worried about the rupiah fall.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma and Tyagita Silka, editing by Sara Webb)  \par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/C.BANK HIGHLIGHT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|IF|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080905e495000me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
