\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Indonesia 2Q Curr Acct In Deficit;First In Nearly 3 Yrs\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2008\par 11:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts lead, adds further details, rupiah's levels and analysts' comments)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia recorded a current account deficit in the second quarter, its first in almost three years, but analysts are confident that the country's economic fundamentals remain sound.\par \par \uc2 The country posted a $1.5 billion deficit in its current account in the second quarter, swinging from a $2.3 billion surplus in the first quarter, Bank Indonesia said in a statement Friday. The current account deficit was the first since the third quarter of 2005 when the country recorded a $1.2 billion deficit.\par \par \uc2 Bank Danamon Chief Economist Anton Gunawan maintained his forecast that the country will record a current account surplus for the entire year. He said a sharp fall in global oil prices recently will likely help improve Indonesia's current account balance. The country has been a net oil importer since 2003.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's balance of payment was in a $1.3 billion surplus in the second quarter, up from $1.0 billion in the January-March period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The balance of payment surplus was due to a $3.7 billion surplus in the capital and financial account, reversing from a $337 million deficit in the first quarter, it added.\par \par \uc2 The surplus in the capital and financial account was due to capital inflows related to portfolio investment, corporate offshore borrowings and foreign direct investment, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The capital inflows were due to an increase in economic activities, an improving investment climate, attractive interest differentials, economic stability, and a positive response from investors on the government's move to hike retail fuel prices in May, it added.\par \par \uc2 Several economists had already expected Indonesia to record a current account deficit in the second quarter due to the 51% on-year rise in imports outpacing export growth of 28% during the period.\par \par \uc2 The current account deficit may undermine the rupiah in the present environment, said \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  Friday, referring to the current selloff in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the rupiah closed at IDR9,395 against the dollar Friday, down from IDR9,250 Thursday. The rupiah's intraday fall Friday to IDR9390 prompted Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but its move failed to reverse the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , however, said that it remains broadly confident with the underlying Indonesian story.\par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia has proven perhaps the most determined \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, issuing a series of hikes and hawkish policy statements, backed by a relatively strong performing local economy," it said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to protect the rupiah with consistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it noted.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier Friday that its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $58.36 billion as of Aug. 29 from $60.56 billion July 31 due to a number of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help bolster the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and partial repayment of the government's offshore debt.\par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 05-09-08 0945GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080905e495000me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
