\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia slides, c.banks step in to prop  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2008\par 05:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended losses against a broadly stronger U.S. dollar on Tuesday, prompting central banks in Thailand, Malaysia, Indonesia, India and the Philippines to defend their struggling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Thailand's deepening political turmoil put additional pressure on the Thai baht <THB=TH>, which fell 0.6 percent to a one-year low at 34.49 per dollar, as traders cited dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The baht <THB=W> dipped to 34.52 in offshore trading.\par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Samak Sundaravej declared a state of emergency in Bangkok on Tuesday and gave the army control of public order after overnight clashes between pro- and anti-government protesters.\par \par \uc2  "This will definitely rub investors the wrong way, and we are likely to see pressure on Thai assets and a weaker Thai baht - the offshore baht markets have already given a good indication of what can be expected," said Vishnu Varathan, economist at Forecast in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  The onshore baht was likely to fall below 34.50 per dollar soon before getting some technical support at 34.75, he added.\par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> fell 0.7 percent to as low as 3.4260 per dollar, its weakest level in a year, and traders suspected the central was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the ringgit.\par \par \uc2  Official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also spotted in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the rupiah <IDR=> fell to a two-week low at 9,196 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  "It's not large. I think they realise that there is no point \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in a dollar bull market," said a Jakarta-based trader.\par \par \uc2  STRONGER DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a 10-month high against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY>, boosted by a sharp drop in oil prices on expectations that Hurricane Gustav's damage to U.S. energy facilities may be smaller than feared.\par \par \uc2  The dollar's rally also weighed on other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Indian rupee <INR=IN> falling to 44.47 per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars to stem the rupee's slide.\par \par \uc2  Such dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has become routine in recent months, helped the Philippine peso <PHP=> stabilise at 46.60 per dollar, its weakest level in almost a year.\par \par \uc2  "The market is definitely and decisively for the dollar, so there is nothing they (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) can do, but they are still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  just like all the other central banks," said a trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a fresh four-year low at 1,133.9 per dollar, down nearly 1.6 percent from the domestic close on Monday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled 3 percent.\par \par \uc2  A wave of capital outflows fuelled by concerns about the fallout of the global credit crisis and high oil prices have hit Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing most of them into the red this year.\par \par \uc2  The won is the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, having shed around 17 percent so far this year, followed by the Philippine peso and Indian rupee, both have fallen by around 11 percent.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0822 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.51         107.74       -0.71\par  Sing dlr        1.4306         1.4233       -0.51\par  Taiwan dlr      31.750         31.593       -0.49\par  Korean won     1132.90        1115.50       -1.54\par  Baht             34.48          34.27       -0.61\par  Peso             46.60          46.29       -0.67\par  Rupiah         9195.00        9158.00       -0.40\par  Rupee            44.42          44.18       -0.54\par  Ringgit         3.4250         3.4020       -0.67\par  Yuan            6.8432         6.8256       -0.26\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.51         111.33       +2.60\par  Sing dlr        1.4306         1.4382       +0.53\par  Taiwan dlr      31.750         32.443       +2.18\par  Korean won     1132.90         935.70      -17.41\par  Baht             34.48          33.68       -2.32\par  Peso             46.60          41.28      -11.42\par  Rupiah         9195.00        9390.00       +2.12\par  Rupee            44.42          39.41      -11.28\par  Ringgit         3.4250         3.3050       -3.50\par  Yuan            6.8432         7.3041       +6.74\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \