\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia, Philippines, Korea c.banks sold dlrs-traders\b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2008\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 27 (Reuters) - Central banks in Indonesia, the Philippines, South Korea and Taiwan were suspected of selling dollars on Tuesday to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure from rising oil prices and falling stock markets, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Three Manila-based traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars around 43.70 per dollar, although the peso <PHP=> still fell to a low of 43.73.\par \par \uc2 "The BSP is providing some offers. I guess they must have sold around 200 million (dollars)," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia was also suspected of selling dollars between 9,365 and 9,380 rupiah per dollar, two traders in Jakarta said. A trader in Singapore also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The state bank has been selling (dollars) quite aggressively this morning from the 9,380-per-U.S. dollar level. I expect it's from BI," a trader in Jakarta said.\par \par \uc2 Traders in Taiwan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <TWD=TP>, which fell for a third consecutive session [nTP259056].\par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities would have sold up to $800 million to lift the won <KRW=>, traders said. [nSEO339974]. (Reporting by Vidya Ranganathan and Melissa Chia; Editing by Tomasz Janowski) ((vidya.ranganathan@thomsonreuters.com; +65-68703090; Reuters Messaging: vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|IF|PHD|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080527e45r0004o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
