\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia rupiah pricing in risk of policy let-down\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan   \par \uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2008\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 14 (Reuters) - A simultaneous bearish move in Indonesian yields and rupiah forwards indicates market participants are betting interest rates will rise but not fast enough to prevent inflation from undermining the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Offshore investors now expect the rupiah <IDR=> to hit 9,850 per dollar within a year, nearly 6 percent weaker than current spot levels at 9,825.\par \par \uc2 Inter-bank one-year rates <JIBOR=BIIA> are just above 9 percent, pricing in at least 75 basis points more of rate rises by Bank Indonesia over the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the offshore non-deliverable forward curve <IDRNDFOR=> is at its steepest in more than two years. Spreads between 3-month and one-year dollar/rupiah levels are at 460 points.\par \par \uc2 That, analysts say, shows that while Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could keep the rupiah tightly bound in the short term, it may be unable to contain longer-term downward pressures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising inflation and portfolio outflows.\par \par \uc2 "The market is hoping for the best but is attaching a risk premium to the rupiah," said Claudio Piron, \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia raised rates last week after inflation hit a 19-month high and long after analysts had warned it was behind the curve and sacrificing an inflation-fighting policy mandate in pursuit of growth.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION WORRY\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's annual inflation, already near 9 percent, is expected to hit double-digit levels if the government follows through on a plan to raise domestically controlled fuel prices.\par \par \uc2 The 25 basis-point rate rise on May 6 raised expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will strive to keep prices stable.\par \par \uc2 But market participants, familiar with the street protests and the rupiah's tumble that followed a fuel price rise in 2005, are nonetheless worried the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be reluctant to do enough to keep inflation under control.\par \par \uc2 Those worries have translated into a higher longer-term implied volatility on rupiah <IDRVOL> and a weaker rupiah in the offshore forwards.\par \par \uc2 "It comes down to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility, and the anticipated sequence of events," said one Hong Kong-based analyst.\par \par \uc2 "If you think that Bank Indonesia will fall behind the curve, and the rupiah will sell off, then Bank Indonesia will tighten as a reaction to that sell-off, then you can be bearish both rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Apart from a possible foot-dragging \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , other factors could weigh on the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia has among the highest pass-throughs in the region from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inflation, making it imperative that Bank Indonesia defends the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it wants to rein in prices.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Piron estimates that even with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $58 billion, Bank Indonesia can cover only 7 months of imports, roughly the same average monthly reserves-to-import ratio that it had in 2005.\par \par \uc2 "It appears that Bank Indonesia looks better placed and highly motivated to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability relative to some of its regional peers," Piron said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "This is not to say that the rupiah is without risk or that the market is oblivious." (Editing by Neil Fullick) ((vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; +65-68703090; Reuters Messaging: vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDONESIA/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080514e45e000zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
