\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Boediono Named As Next Bank Indonesia Governor   \b0\par\par\uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2008\par 14:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds Boediono comments on inflation, quotes from parliamentarian, background.) \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--A commission of the Indonesian parliament Monday named senior economic minister Boediono as the country's next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, an appointment that is set to restore confidence in a corruption-tainted Bank Indonesia, and bolster investor confidence in the Southeast Asian nation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 "Some heavy challenges will face Boediono in synchronizing monetary policy with the fiscal authorities, and in tackling the difficulties with our national economy which is under strong pressures both from internal and global (factors)," said Awal Kusumah, head of Parliamentary Commission 11, which reviewed potential appointees to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor position.   \par \par \uc2 The appointment is subject to a plenary hearing April 9, which will be presided over by house speaker Agus Laksono, Kusumah told reporters after a day-long hearing.   \par \par \uc2 In previous appointments of Bank Indonesia governors, the plenary hearing has been little more than a formalizing of the parliamentary commission's candidate.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono, who like many Indonesians is known by only one name, will be sworn in as the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief on May 17 when the incumbent, Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah, finishes his five-year term.   \par \par \uc2 Abdullah opted not to seek re-election after the Anti-Corruption Body in February named him as a suspect in a corruption investigation that has embroiled several other senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. Abdullah has denied any wrongdoing.   \par \par \uc2 "The markets really respect Boediono," said Standard Chartered Economist Fauzi Ichsan. "He is the most qualified person (to head Bank Indonesia)."   \par \par \uc2 President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono last week proposed Boediono - who has an extensive track record in managing the economy - after parliament last month rejected two candidates for what they said was a lack of relevant experience.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono, a graduate of the University of Pennsylvania's Wharton School, was a director at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the mid to late 1990s. His latter experience could smooth decision making at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , current governor Abdullah said.   \par \par \uc2 In pre-appointment hearings to parliament Monday, Boediono vowed to improve morale at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to work hard to combat inflation which threatens to breach Bank Indonesia's target this year.   \par \par \uc2 "The current inflation targeting system that Bank Indonesia uses now could be perfected," Boediono said without elaborating.   \par \par \uc2 He said that the key for the achievement of the inflation target is "the credibility of the target itself, measures taken to achieve it and the institutional credibility of Bank Indonesia itself."   \par \par \uc2 Like many countries around the world, Indonesia is facing mounting inflationary pressures stemming from soaring global food and energy prices. Bank Indonesia has admitted that could mean inflation heading a little beyond its 6.5% target for the year but many analysts believe that is overly optimistic.   \par \par \uc2 Just last month, the consumer price index spiked to 8.2% on year, the fastest rise in prices for 18 months. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reluctant to raise its 8.0% interest rates, arguing that external, not internal, conditions were behind the high inflation rate.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Boediono might not alter that stance any time soon.   \par \par \uc2 "Balancing the pressures of higher inflation and a potential global slowdown, he will find it appropriate to take a wait-and-see approach on interest rates," said David Cohen, chief economist at Singapore-based Action Economics. Bank Indonesia next meets to discuss interest rates on May 8.   \par \par \uc2 But he forecast Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the rupiah against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Besides tackling inflation, Boediono also said Monday that Bank Indonesia needs to form a task force to improve budgetary decision making to prevent a recurrence of the corruption allegations now surrounding several \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials.   \par \par \uc2 The allegations concern alleged illegal transfer of funds from a Bank Indonesia foundation to several former members of parliament.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono said that he has never illegally taken "even one cent of the public's money," and said he aims to stamp out the culture of corruption that remains so prevalent in Indonesia that even a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor became a graft suspect.   \par \par \uc2 "Throughout the length of my career, and God-willing until I die, I hope I can continue to maintain this characteristic" of being immune to corruption, Boediono said.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono's departure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves an opening at the head of President Yudhoyono's economic team at a time of persistent turbulence in world financial markets and economies.   \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's government has been criticized of late for a lack of policies to deal with a rising budget deficit, inflated by ballooning energy subsidies.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono also said that the rupiah is currently satisfactorily stable against the dollar, and said that over the coming years Indonesia should be able to achieve an inflation rate more closely in line with regional peers.   \par \par \uc2 He said that "in the next few years," he hopes Indonesia will lower inflation to around 3% to 4%.   \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Linda Silaen and Reuben Carder; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com, Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 07-04-08 1259GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080407e447000s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
