\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Shares Fall 4.5%; Inflation Concerns Mount   \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2008\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's share market has fallen sharply Thursday as investors grow concerned that rising inflation will start to take a bite out of economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 The share declines have been exacerbated by margin calls with the market now down a total of 8.8% over three days.   \par \par \uc2 Jakarta's benchmark share index was recently 4.5% lower at 2,237.92 with trading volume on the heavy side at a value of IDR3.5 trillion.   \par \par \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas expects the JSX index to find some support at 2200, though its head of research, Ari Pitoyo, said any break below this level could push the index towards the 1700 to 1800 range.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have been selling, concerned about the inflation outlook after data earlier in the week showed a spike in price pressures. There are worries that Jakarta lacks the policy options for dealing decisively with inflation, especially with the rupiah falling and a widening budget deficit. "Our macroeconomic fundamentals look weaker with inflation rising," said Andreas Yasakasih, a fund manager at PT Ciptadana Asset Management.   \par \par \uc2 Investors likely to have been hit by margin calls include those holding shares of Bumi Resources (BUMI.JK); its shares were down 6.5% after it booked only $473 million in gains from the sale of coal assets in 2007, less than the expected $553 million.   \par \par \uc2 Bumi shares were also lower because investors had been looking to raise cash in order to subscribe to a rights share offer at  \uc2 Bakrie & Brothers\uc2  (BNBR.JK), which will use the proceeds to buy Bumi stock and that of other affiliates.   \par \par \uc2 Heavyweight  \uc2 PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia\uc2  (TLKM.JK) meanwhile was down 3.6%, with  \uc2 Astra International\uc2  (ASII.JK) 7.7% lower on concerns higher inflation will hurt car and motorcycle demand.   \par \par \uc2 The consumer price index in March rose 0.95% on month and 8.17% on year, well above expectations in a Dow Jones Newswires poll for a rise of 0.31% on month and 7.46% on year.   \par \par \uc2 The data follow above-target numbers for January and February and economists say this suggests the government may have a hard time meeting its full-year inflation target of 4% to 6.5%.   \par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires poll of 12 economists shows the general expectation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep interest rates on hold at its meeting Thursday, with the benchmark one-month rate now at 8%.   \par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered bank added "in the aftermath of the meeting, Bank Indonesia may signal that near term rate cuts are off the table."   \par \par \uc2 Indeed, given inflationary pressures, there will be growing expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eventually be forced to raise rates, it said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah meanwhile has weakened further, hurt by fund outflows from stocks and the bond market. Recently, the U.S. dollar was trading around IDR9,230 compared to IDR9,215 Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "We have many orders from our foreign clients investing in the stock and bond markets to buy the dollar," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer, who added Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rupiah fell further.   \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to trade in a IDR9,225-IDR9,240 range for the rest of the session.   \par \par \uc2 -by Jakarta bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4141; rosalind.mathieson@dowjones.com [ 03-04-08 0529GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 5055 55109   \par \par \uc2 Dokument