\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Indonesia Leaves 1-Month Rate Unchanged At 8%   \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2008\par 08:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes and comments on the outlook for interest rates and the rupiah, and analysts' comments)   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia left its benchmark one-month interest rate unchanged at 8% Tuesday due to concerns about rising inflationary pressures, but it said there is still room for cuts later this year.   \par \par \uc2 "According to Bank Indonesia's evaluation, inflationary pressures in 2008 will be quite strong," Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said at a press conference after a monthly board of governors' meeting.   \par \par \uc2 Economists say rising oil and commodity prices globally and the rupiah's recent weakness are likely to drive prices of goods higher in the coming months.   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia is targeting an inflation rate between 4% and 6% this year, down from 6.59% in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Senior Deputy Governor Miranda Goeltom said that "looking at the current situation, we still see room for rate cuts in the future. But (we) can't say yet when they will happen as we must see monthly developments in the economy."   \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect the one-month rate to remain at 8% until the end of the first half of the year at least, but views on the outlook for interest rates later in the year are mixed.   \par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be forced to raise the official rate by 150 basis points this year to rein in inflation, and such increases would be very negative for the local stock market.   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia has cut rates a total 475 basis points in an easing cycle that began in May 2006. The rate cuts have helped to spur commercial bank lending, which rose 23% on year during the first 11 months of 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Governor Abdullah said Tuesday that the rupiah was less sensitive to global oil price movements last year than in previous years. He didn't elaborate, but oil price increases have had less effect on confidence since the government cut local price subsidies in October 2005.   \par \par \uc2 The average exchange rate of the U.S. dollar last year was IDR9,140, versus IDR9,197 in 2006, even though global oil prices continued to rise, Abdullah said.   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the rupiah comes under selling pressure, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah was rising in the first half of the year, but it has tended to weaken since risk aversion rose following the U.S. subprime mortgage crisis. At 0740 GMT, the dollar was quoted at IDR9,452, little changed from Monday's close of IDR9447.   \par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna and I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 08-01-08 0747GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080108e418000cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
