\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 22   \b0\par\par\uc2 1,726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2007\par 08:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.   \par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE:BOJ NAKAMURA WARNS ON SUBPRIME IMPACT; NO POLICY HINT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan board member Seiji Nakamura said Thursday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must carefully monitor the impact of the U.S. subprime-loan crisis, suggesting that he doesn't see an imminent need to raise interest rates. (published 0354 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MIN TO KEEP CLOSE EYE ON RISING YEN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Thursday reminded market participants that authorities are closely monitoring the yen's rise against the dollar, but offered no clear sign that the nation is considering \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0139 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STATISTICS HEAD SEES 2007 GDP GROWTH AROUND 11.5%    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China economy is likely to grow around 11.5% this year, said Xie Fuzhan, director of the National Bureau of Statistics, on Thursday. (published 0653 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBI MOHAN: INDIA INSULATED FROM EXTERNAL SHOCKS SO FAR    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is insulated from external shocks arising mainly from subprime credit problems in the U.S., the Reserve Bank of India's Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan said Thursday. (published 0512 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SLOWDOWN NOT TO HURT MEDIUM TERM INDIA GROWTH-GOVT EXEC    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A slowdown in the U.S. economy won't have an impact on India's growth in the medium term, the deputy chairman of the Planning Commission, which advises the federal government on economic policy, said Thursday. (published 0541 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: HOPE EU CAN EASE CURBS ON HIGH-TECH EXPORTS TO CHINA    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China hopes the European Union can ease restrictions on high-technology exports to China, Wang Xinpei, spokesman for China's Ministry of Commerce, said during a press briefing Thursday. (published 0247 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: CLOSELY WATCHING FINANCIAL MARKET MOVEMENTS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Thursday it is closely monitoring volatile financial market movements stemming from renewed attention to subprime mortgage woes and rising global risk aversion. (published 0227 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF KOREA CHANGES MONETARY STABILIZATION BOND LIMIT RULE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Thursday that it is changing a rule that set a limit to monetary stabilization bond issues, a move which the market is interpreting as a step towards tightening market liquidity. (published 0326 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:BANK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDONESIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF RUPIAH FALLS TOO FAST    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the rupiah falls "too fast" against the dollar. (published 0140 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GOVT RESEARCH: YEN CARRY TRADE RISK FOR CHINA STABILITY    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any large unwinding of Japanese yen carry trades could pose significant risks to China's financial stability and the yuan, according to a recent research paper published by China's Ministry of Commerce. (published 0515 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA WILL CLOSELY WATCH US TRADE PROBES ON CHINESE EXPORTS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Thursday it will "closely observe" further U.S. investigations of claims that some Chinese exports are subsidized and sold below cost, and will protect its interests and the lawful rights of Chinese companies. (published 0459 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF NUKAGA: WILL FULFILL RESPONSIBILITY AS FIN MIN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga on Thursday reiterated he didn't attend a controversial dinner with an arrested former official of a scandal-hit trade company, and indicated he has no plans to step down. (published 0358 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ FIN MIN: RBNZ SHOULD RETAIN FOCUS ON FIGHTING INFLATION    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen said Thursday he strongly believes the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's must retain its focus on fighting inflation, adding that a review of monetary policy by a parliament select committee will take some time to complete. (published 2209 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S COSTELLO: BANKS SHOULD ABSORB ADDED CREDIT COST    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Peter Costello repeated Thursday his recent warnings to local banks not to pass on higher wholesale funding costs to consumers via higher variable mortgage interest rates. (published 0144 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA LIKELY TO KEEP POLICY RATES UNCHANGED MON    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will almost certainly keep its overnight policy rate unchanged at its last rate-setting meeting for the year on Monday, but economists are divided over the outlook for the benchmark rate in 2008. (published 0505 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS:AUSTRALIA BANKS MAY RAISE HOME RATES; KEEP RBA ON HOLD    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's banks are likely to move quickly to raise mortgage interest rates after Saturday's federal election as pressure on wholesale market funding costs intensify due to renewed global market volatility and risk aversion. (published 0501 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: CHINA LOSES APPETITE FOR INTEREST RATE HIKES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There won't be a Friday night announcement from the People's  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 , it seems: The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in no hurry to raise interest rates for the sixth time this year. (published 2356 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =AUSSIE VOTE: NO MATTER WHO WINS, ECONOMY SET FOR BOOST    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No matter who wins Australia's federal election Saturday, a spending spree promised by both major political parties ensures that the economy and inflation will receive a boost, encouraging the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to further tighten monetary policy. (published 0155 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: CHECKING THE BALANCE IN THE AUSSIE SENATE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian election this weekend may yet put the Senate in the hands of the opposition parties, which wouldn't be a terrible thing, really. (published 2308 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FUJITSU JUL-SEP GROUP NET PROFIT Y5.4B VS Y14.2B PROFIT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fujitsu Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday its net profit for the July-September quarter dropped 62% due to a heavier tax burden on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the U.K. (published 0634 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:  \f28 \uc2 \f2 JAPAN TOBACCO\f28 \uc2 \f2 , NISSIN FOOD TO BUY KATOKICHI    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Tobacco Inc.\f28 \uc2 \f2  and instant noodle maker  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissin Food Products Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday they will jointly buy Katokichi Co. in a deal exceeding Y100 billion, hoping to create the leader in Japan's frozen food industry. (published 0541 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIO BEAUTY GROUP SEEKS UP TO US$309 MLN IN HK IPO-TERM SHEET    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bio Beauty Group Ltd., a spinoff of  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Global Green Tech Group Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is seeking to raise up to US$309 million in an initial public offering ahead of listing in Hong Kong next month, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Thursday. (published 0433 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW:  \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASIANA AIRLINES\f28 \uc2 \f2  AIMS FOR OVER KRW4T SALES IN 2008    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Asiana Airlines Inc. is targeting sales of over KRW4 trillion in 2008 by stepping up its efforts to increase routes to China and the U.S. as well as starting a service to Paris. (published 0532 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ARCELORMITTAL HAS LONG POSITION OF 73.1% IN CHINA ORIENTAL    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2  has increased its long position in  \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Oriental Group Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  to 73.1% from 28.0%, the company said in a filing to the Hong Kong stock exchange, though it is unclear whether the position reflects an actual rise in shareholding. (published 0356 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NOR OFFSHORE PLANS TO RAISE US$150M IN SINGAPORE IPO-SOURCES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Offshore vessel operator NOR Offshore Ltd. plans to raise about US$150 million in a Singapore initial public offering, two people familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0429 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: F&P HEALTHCARE 1H NET FALLS; NZD TO WEIGH ON FY    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fisher & Paykel Healthcare Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2  Thursday reported a sharp 29% fall in fiscal first-half net profit and said a strong New Zealand dollar will hurt full-year earnings. (published 0029 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KEPCO\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO CUT KRW450B IN EXPENSES TO OFFSET OIL PRICES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Kepco, said Thursday it plans to cut its general expenses by KRW450 billion by the end of this year to cope with surging global oil prices. (published 0335 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:DAEWOO ELEC "PRIME BIDDERS" TO BE NAMED BY JAN-SOURCE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Creditors of  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Electronics Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2  Thursday put the South Korean company up for sale again after talks to sell it to a consortium led by India's  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Videocon Industries Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  failed in May due to price differences. (published 0647 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOLHURST: MACQUARIE PROPOSES TO BUY 19.4% STAKE IN TOLHURST    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  has proposed to buy 19.4% of the issued capital in stock broker  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tolhurst Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  by way of a placement and a share acquisition, Tolhurst said Thursday. (published 0018 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: TUI OIL RESERVE BOOSTED, PRODUCTION TARGET UPPED    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Worldwide Exploration Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  and  \f28 \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Oil & Gas Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  Thursday boosted its estimate of oil reserves at the Tui joint venture by 30% and raised the production target for the project. (published 0250 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEXUS ENERGY SAYS ANZON MERGER A COMPELLING OPTION    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nexus Energy Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  Thursday again raised the prospect of a merger with  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anzon Australia Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which it said would create Australia's leading mid-tier oil and gas company. (published 0041 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDOSAT 9-MONTH NET IDR1.44 TLN VS IDR927.17 BLN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Indonesia Satellite Corp. Thursday reported a 55% on-year rise in its nine-month net profit, due to an increase in revenue. (published 0519 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INVESTIGATION FINDS MACQUARIE BK BREACHED  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MEDIA CONTROL\f28 \uc2 \f2  RULES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Bank Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its directors won't face charges despite an investigation by the Australian Communications and Media Authority finding a breach of federal media control rules. (published 2226 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECUADOR PRES SHRUGS OFF CHINA ARBITRATION THREAT OVER OIL TAX    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ecuador President Rafael Correa shrugged off a potential arbitration suit from China's oil firms over his country's new windfall tax, and criticized the international system for solving commercial disputes as serving Western interests. (published 0530 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT: SIGNED NUCLEAR COOPERATION PACT WITH INDONESIA    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese and Indonesian governments have signed a memorandum of cooperation on nuclear energy, Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Thursday. (published 0359 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM OKS LONG-TERM PLANS TO BOOST BIOFUEL PRODUCTION    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-11-07 0715GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Vietnamese government has approved long-term plans to boost biofuel production, which will account for 5% of the country's total petroleum demand by 2025. (published 0323 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE TIN CO OBTAINS EXPORT LICENSE FOR INDONESIAN OPS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Tin Industries' Indonesian joint venture has obtained a license to export refined tin and will begin shipping 1,000 metric tons in December, a senior company official said Thursday. (published 0425 GMT) [ 22-11-07 0715GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071122e3bm0009s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
