\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Selective gains as weak stocks, risk weigh   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan   \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2007\par 03:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar and Philippine peso rose on Monday against a tumbling U.S. dollar but other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had difficulty appreciating as regional stock markets fell and concerns over credit markets intensified.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell against the yen <JPY=> and hit a 12-year low against the Swiss franc <CHF=>, battered by weak industrial production data on Friday and worries about credit-related losses at financial institutions.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said some of the selling pressure on the dollar arose after a source familiar with Saudi Arabian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy told Reuters the world's largest oil exporter could consider revaluing its dollar-pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nL19685742]   \par \par \uc2 The credit market concerns weighed on investor sentiment and appetite for risk and led to weakness in Asian stock markets <0#.INDEXA>.   \par \par \uc2 MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> fell slightly on Monday. Last week, it dropped 3.4 percent, marking its third consecutive week of losses.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> barely gained 0.3 percent, even after the government raised its economic growth forecast for 2008 and forecast higher inflation rates. [ID:nSIN258187]. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to 1.4459 per U.S. dollar and then retreated to 1.4483.   \par \par \uc2 "You'd have thought the market would have reacted a bit more positively to that," said  \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  strategist Simon Flint.   \par \par \uc2 "But people are using the Singapore dollar as the most liquid proxy for their risk aversion fears and growth fears," he said, adding investors held sizeable short dollar position but were also looking to reduce or hedge some of their risk in other markets.   \par \par \uc2 "We're bearish on the dollar. What's going on in the Middle East is quite meaningful," Flint said.   \par \par \uc2 He said he expected an eventual appreciation in the Singapore dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The Asian decoupling story is very much alive and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has got quite an aggressive and forward-looking appreciation stance," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The high-yielding Philippine peso <PHP=> rose as far as 43.19 per dollar, up 0.8 percent from Friday's close. Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely moved.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> was steady around 9,320 per dollar, while the Indian rupee <INR=IN> kept to a tight range around 39.3 per dollar.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to prop up the rupiah <IDR=> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is prepared to take more action if necessary, deputy governor Hartadi Sarwono told Reuters on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Sarwono also repeated that the fall in the rupiah, Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar so far this year, was likely to be temporary.   \par \par \uc2 Last week, the high-yielders led a broad retreat in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside falling stocks, undermined by persistent concerns about the fallout from the U.S. subprime market crisis. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0822 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest b