\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia's high-yielders rally, mood still cautious   \b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2007\par 05:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuters) - The high-yielding Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso rose on Wednesday in cautious trade amid growing hopes the Federal Reserve will cut its main interest rate to calm turbulent markets.   \par \par \uc2 The peso went as far as 46.50 per dollar, up almost 0.9 percent from Tuesday's close.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> gained 0.6 percent to 9,380 per dollar, while the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> followed by rising half of a percent to about 3.48 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "We're finally seeing the short-term relief. I think there was some lag effect on the dollar/peso side and the pressure in the offshore market seems to be easing as well," said a trader in Manila.   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Burhanuddin Abdullah said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah and expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise at around 9,000 in coming weeks.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said investors remained edgy after last week's heavy battering, but prospects of a near-term U.S. rate cut offered support to share and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 "Cautious tone remains. It's range trading with some dollar/Asia downside bias on equity market stability," said Han Sia Yeo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 Bank of America.\par \par \uc2 "However, with market positioned for a Fed cut near-term, risk is on the upside for dollar/Asia for now," he said.   \par \par \uc2 A senior U.S. lawmaker said on Tuesday Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke assured him the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would use "all available tools" to calm financial markets, which investors took as a signal the Fed could cut rates at its Sept. 18 meeting.   \par \par \uc2 In a sign of improved sentiment MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> rose 1.4 percent, But Richmond Federal Reserve Bank President Jeffrey Lacker poured some cold water on rate cut hopes, saying market turmoil only warranted a change in rates if it affected the outlook for inflation or growth.   \par \par \uc2 NO YUAN SURPRISE   \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> fell 0.16 percent to 7.6031 per dollar -- still off its six-week low of 7.6099 hit on Friday -- after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates for the fourth time this year in its campaign to curb rising inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect Chinese leaders to stick to their long-standing policy of letting the yuan appreciate only gradually in the run-up to a Communist Party congress later this year.   \par \par \uc2 "Although a stronger yuan will be able to offset higher price trends, major reform is unlikely ahead of sensitive political events this autumn,"  \uc2 UBS\uc2  analysts said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen, which has moved in the opposite direction to most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks, held gains against the dollar <JPY=> as investors continued to cut risky positions.   \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=>, South Korean won <KRW=> and Indian rupee <INR=IN> were the most negatively correlated to the yen's recent swings, DBS analysts said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=> and Singapore dollar, which were little changed in afternoon trade, were least responsive to the yen's changes as investors used them as an alternative funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for carry trades, they said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0730 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.83         114.29       -0.47\par  Sing dlr        1.5273         1.5272       -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.978         32.921       -0.17\par  Korean won      943.90         943.40       -0.05\par  Baht             34.47          34.48       +0.03\par  Peso             46.50          46.90       +0.86\par  Rupiah         9395.00        9435.00       +0.43\par  Rupee            40.95          41.08       +0.32\par  Ringgit         3.4830         3.4965       +0.39\par  Yuan            7.5995         7.5906       -0.12\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.83         119.01       +3.64\par  Sing dlr        1.5273         1.5337       +0.42\par  Taiwan dlr      32.978         32.585       -1.19\par  Korean won      943.90        0929.50       -1.53\par  Baht             34.47          36.08       +4.67\par  Peso             46.50          49.03       +5.44\par  Rupiah         9395.00        8988.00       -4.33\par  Rupee            40.95          44.26       +8.07\par  Ringgit         3.4830         3.5270       +1.26\par  Yuan            7.5995         7.8051       +2.71\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Nina Jay)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070825e38m0004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
