\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia slides to new lows as investors flee risk   \b0\par\par\uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2007\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled to fresh lows on Thursday as regional stocks collapsed and investors cut their exposure to riskier assets due to worries about credit market risk, forcing central banks to continue supporting them.   \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> took the biggest hit, dropping 1.5 percent to a 3-month low near 947 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Other high-yielders such as the Philippine peso <PHP=>, Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> and Indian rupee <INR=IN> also shed up to nearly 1 percent each.   \par \par \uc2  Central banks in Singapore, Malaysia, the Philippines and Indonesia were suspected of selling dollars to slow the declines in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the bearishness seemed deeply entrenched as bad news continued to hit credit markets.   \par \par \uc2  "It's a crazy market here. Prices jump 100 pips in two minutes!" said one trader in Kuala Lumpur.   \par \par \uc2  "I am going to stay long dollars because surely there will be more subprime news every day," he said.   \par \par \uc2  The latest market scare was set off by worries that  \uc2 Countrywide Financial\uc2  , the largest U.S. mortgage lender, could face bankruptcy if liquidity worsens. [ID:nN15253338].   \par \par \uc2  Australian Mortgage lender RAMS Home Loans Group Ltd.  slumped after it said it had failed to roll over short-term loans due to a lack of liquidity in the U.S. commercial paper market. [ID:nSYD33571].   \par \par \uc2  Some Asian stock markets <0#.INDEXA> saw the biggest losses since the Sept. 2001 attacks on the United States.   \par \par \uc2  Central banks around the region assured markets of support. Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also pumped in a larger than usual amount into its money markets.   \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen jumped to a five-month high against the dollar <JPY=> and euro <EURJPY=> as investors unwound carry-trade positions funded by the low-yielding yen.   \par \par \uc2  Traders in Asia said the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have sold up to $700 million as the ringgit <MYR=> hit a March trough of 3.5070 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's dollar selling managed to put a floor on the rupiah around 9,482 per dollar and even nudge the rupiah higher to near 9,450.   \par \par \uc2  "Imported inflation is a key consideration for Bank Indonesia,"  \uc2 UBS\uc2  analysts said in a note.   \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  might intensify its dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupiah approaches 9,500, particularly because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said in the past the acceptable range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is between 8,500 and 9,500 per dollar,  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2  "We expect Bank Indonesia to put up a fight at 9,500, although the generalised rampage into the dollar fuelled by ongoing credit woes may give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  an excuse to tolerate a higher dollar/rupiah if the defence of 9,500 fails,"  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0800 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.08         116.92       +0.72\par  Sing dlr        1.5352         1.5296       -0.36\par  Taiwan dlr      33.128         33.010       -0.36\par  Korean won      946.10         932.00       -1.49