\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Bank Indonesia: Subprime Impact Only On Fin Mkts   \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2007\par 07:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds end-July \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves amount, Bank Indonesia recent rate decision, background on rupiah performance)   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia will make "all-out efforts" to help local financial markets weather the impact of the U.S. subprime market woes, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin said Friday.   \par \par \uc2 This would include \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he indicated.   \par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are strong enough to maintain calm in the market," Tadjuddin said.   \par \par \uc2 The reserves are currently at $52.4 billion, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The reserves stood at $51.88 billion as of July 31, but Tadjuddin didn't explain what drove them higher amid fund outflows from the local financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 He said that the impact of the U.S. subprime market on Indonesia has so far been limited to only the financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 "Our economic fundamentals are quite strong," he said. "There's nothing to worry about."   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Tuesday said that Indonesian banks don't have any exposure to U.S. subprime assets as they aren't allowed to invest in overseas papers.   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia still believes that the government's target for the dollar-rupiah average exchange rate of IDR9,100 for this year is achievable, Tadjuddin said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at IDR9,330 at 0425 GMT, up from its close Thursday at IDR9,305.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has fallen to a one-year low against the dollar as foreign investors are trimming their holdings in local stocks, government bonds and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sertifikat Bank Indonesia papers.   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia on Tuesday decided to keep its one-month key rate at 8.25% in light of the current turbulence in global financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna, contributing to Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 10-08-07 0509GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070810e38a000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
