\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Bank Indonesia Dep Governor:IDR Weakness Is Temporary   \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2007\par 09:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds further comments from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official, background on interest rates.) \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The rupiah's recent slide against the U.S. dollar is temporary and reflects a trend of weakening in emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rather than cracks in Indonesia's economic fundamentals, but Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands "very ready" to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent excess rupiah volatility, a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Monday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin said he was "certain" that the rupiah's weakness won't prevent Indonesia's ability to reach its 2007 inflation target of 5-7%, and predicted that the country's strong domestic fundamentals will likely boost the rupiah again soon, perhaps as early as next week.   \par \par \uc2 "This movement (in the rupiah) I am sure is temporary, and investors' perceptions (of Indonesia) will improve again. I see that overall the rupiah is on a strengthening trend because our economic conditions are good," he told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "very ready" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent excess rupiah volatility, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at IDR9,347 as of 0541 GMT Monday, up sharply from IDR9,075 a week ago.   \par \par \uc2 "The current weakness of the rupiah is temporary in nature. It is due to global and external factors, primarily in America," Tadjuddin said.   \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin didn't elaborate further, but the comments reflect an effort by Indonesian authorities to calm investors nerves, which have been rattled by turmoil in the U.S. subprime mortgage market and ensuing slump in global stocks. Assets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of emerging economies such as Indonesia's have been among the hardest hit by the spike in risk aversion that has swept over global markets in recent weeks, analysts and traders say.   \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are currently around $52 billion, the highest level in the country's history. That means Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has sufficient (reserves) to make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe," Tadjuddin said.   \par \par \uc2 But he said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't targeting a specific range for the rupiah against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 A decision expected Tuesday on interest rates "depends more on internal factors" than on global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, Tadjuddin said.   \par \par \uc2 "We know our macroeconomic conditions are very strong, although we will still also look at external factors" when deciding whether or not to cut borrowing costs, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board of governors are slated to meet Tuesday to determine whether the benchmark interest rate will be changed this month. The one-month policy rate currently stands at 8.25%. Bank Indonesia has slashed the benchmark rate by 450 basis points since headline inflation began to ease in May last year.   \par \par \uc2 However analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stand pat on rates this month due to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness and higher on-year headline inflation in July.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Reuben Carder and Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 06-08-07 0737GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070806e386000et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
