\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah leads stellar gains in Asia   \b0\par\par\uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2007\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 7 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rose more than 1 percent to a one-year high versus the dollar on Monday, leading a strong rally across Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dollar took a blow from weak U.S. jobs data at the end of last week.   \par \par \uc2 Comments in the past few days from some Asian officials suggesting they were not too worried about strength in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelled the rally.   \par \par \uc2 Both the Indian rupee <INR=IN> and Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> hit nine-year peaks, while the Philippine peso <PHP=> rose to a six-year high and the South Korean won <KRW=> climbed 0.6 percent to its highest in more than 4-\u189\'00\'BD months.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> outperformed its Asian peers, building on sharp gains on Friday. It rose as far as 8,855 per dollar, its strongest level since mid-May 2006.   \par \par \uc2 It had lagged gains in its Asian peers, but market focus has now returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on renewed interest in carry trades, talk of another cut in Indonesian interest rates and signs that Jakarta will not stand in the way of rupiah strength.   \par \par \uc2 In the past three sessions, the rupiah has shot up 2 percent, triggering a jump in rupiah implied volatility <IDRVOL>, a measure of expectations about the size of future market moves.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to focus on at the moment is the rupiah," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank. "It has been the laggard in regional gains. Also, the message from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be that there will not be so much \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow markets to determine the rupiah rate, even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened beyond 9,000 per dollar. The rupiah broke through that level shortly after his comments.   \par \par \uc2 A Jakarta trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been spotted in the market on Monday buying dollars for rupiah to smooth a volatile market but said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared small.   \par \par \uc2 "They are still there, but only buying dollars in small amounts," he said. "There are strong flows from offshore into the bonds and interest rates market."   \par \par \uc2 Indonesian President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono is expected to announce a cabinet reshuffle later on Monday, but this is not seen having a significant impact on the rupiah.[ID:nJAK215355]   \par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also bolstered by strong gains in local shares -- Taiwan's stock index <.TWII> hit a 6-\u189\'00\'BD year high, while shares in Singapore <.STI> and Korea <.KS11> rose to record peaks.   \par \par \uc2 LAISSEZ FAIRE   \par \par \uc2 Weekend comments from Asian officials at an Asian Development Bank meeting in Japan also helped drive regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.   \par \par \uc2 The strength of Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not affecting its exports because they are fundamentally competitive, the country's Second Finance Minister Nor Mohamed Yakcop said on Sunday.   \par \par \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Amando Tetangco indicated on Sunday that the strong peso was not a concern as it reflected the nation's improved economic performance and helped tame inflation.   \par \par \uc2 The ringgit rose to a nine-year high at about 3.4135 per dollar, while the peso gained almost a quarter of a percent to a six-year peak around 47.35 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "We expect strong inflows from remittances and follow through selling of the dollar after the payrolls data, are behind the peso move," said a trader in Manila. "The Tetangco comments should also boost the peso today."   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. economy added a lower-than-expected 88,000 jobs in April, data showed on Friday, reinforcing expectations the Federal Reserve will cut interest rates later this year. The Fed is expected to hold the federal funds rate steady at 5.25 percent when it meets on May 9.   \par \par \uc2 Markets in Thailand and China were closed for a holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0747 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.91         120.34       +0.36\par  Sing dlr        1.5130         1.5197       +0.44\par  Taiwan dlr      33.237         33.280       +0.13\par  Korean won      922.30         927.50       +0.56\par  Baht             34.73          34.74       +0.03\par  Peso             47.35          47.46       +0.24\par  Rupiah         8870.00        8970.00       +1.13\par  Rupee            40.60          40.86       +0.64\par  Ringgit         3.4135         3.4200       +0.19\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.91         119.01       -0.75\par  Sing dlr        1.5130         1.5337       +1.37\par  Taiwan dlr      33.237         32.585       -1.96\par  Korean won      922.30        0929.50       +0.78\pa