\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Econ Min: Won't Hold Down IDR; Level 'Realistic'   \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2007\par 09:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian government won't hold down the rupiah, which has strengthened to 12-month highs against the dollar, as the level is 'still realistic,' a senior minister said Monday.   \par \par \uc2 'It (the rupiah's rise) is due to market forces,' Coordinating Minister for the Economy Boediono told reporters. 'We shouldn't fight against the market...we shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .'   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so long as daily volatility doesn't exceed 2%.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono said that the rupiah's rise was due to the dollar's weakness and capital inflows to Indonesian financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was traded at IDR8,945 at 0700 GMT, down from its close Friday at IDR9,030. The greenback fell to an intraday low of IDR8,855 before profit-taking against the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  set in.   \par \par \uc2 Boediono said that the rupiah level is still good for exports and imports. -By Linda Silaen; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Graham Norris   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070507e357002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
