\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Bk Indonesia: Thai Moves "Nothing To Worry About" For IDR  \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2006\par 10:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The stability of the Indonesian rupiah isn't under any immediate threat from the type of speculative activity that recently sent the Thai baht to a nine-year high against the U.S. dollar, a senior Bank Indonesia official said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We have sufficient regulations to curb any speculative moves...and more-than-sufficient \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves (to defend the rupiah)," Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 But Tadjuddin said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "always in the market" and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to protect the rupiah from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators.  \par \par \uc2 At 0730 GMT, the dollar was trading at IDR9,178, down from an intraday high of IDR9,203, but considerably higher than Monday's close of IDR9,084.  \par \par \uc2 The situation in Thailand was "nothing to worry about" for the rupiah due to existing laws that curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation activities, Tadjuddin said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia also has around $41 billion in foreign reserves it can deploy to protect the local unit, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin said Indonesia's regulations, including a 2005 rule that restricts rupiah transactions and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lending, meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "needn't follow suit" and emulate the Bank of Thailand's capital control measures.  \par \par \uc2 "The (existing) regulation is sufficient to prevent the market from speculative trading," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand from Tuesday has imposed new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls to prevent the baht from appreciating sharply after speculative inflows pushed the unit to a nine-year high.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin said the recent spike in the value of the baht against the dollar and the Bank of Thailand's moves would likely have only a temporary regional impact.  \par \par \uc2 Normal regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions would likely resume "after the market knows what's happening in Thailand," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna contributing to Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020061219e2cj003eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
