\par\par \b \uc2 Bk Indonesia: Dollar Likely At IDR9,000-IDR9,500 In 2007  \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2006\par 03:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar will likely move between IDR9,000 and IDR9,500 in 2007, with an average exchange rate of IDR9,300, Bank Indonesia said Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't give further details to back its prognosis on the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 The market will likely take the forecast as an indication of the range Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is comfortable with and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair trades outside that band.  \par \par \uc2 At 0220 GMT, the dollar was trading at IDR9,106. [ 11-12-06 0223GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 A Bank Indonesia handout distributed in a seminar on Shariah banking reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast of 6.1% economic growth next year, slightly below the government's 6.3% target.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it expects inflation next year at 6.5%.  \par \par \uc2 "Further rate cuts in 2007 will hinge on inflation and macroeconomic stability," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week cut its benchmark rate by 50 basis points to 9.75% as inflation continues to ease.  \par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 11-12-06 0241GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061211e2cb0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
