IN 2006 - C.BANK  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia said on Thursday it predicted the country's economy to expand by 5.4 percent year-on-year in the third quarter and wrapped the year with 5.5 percent growth of its gross domestic product (GDP).  \par \par \uc2 - BANK NIAGA PROJECTS 25 PERCENT RISE IN NET PROFIT  \par \par \uc2 Indonesian lender, PT Bank Niaga Tbk , was projecting a 25 percent increase in its net profit this year, partly helped by the declining trend in the country's interest rates, its president director said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 - HOTEL SAHID SEEKS 500 BLN RUPIAH FUNDS  \par \par \uc2 Indonesian-based hotel chain, PT Hotel Sahid Jaya Internasional Tbk , was seeking to raise between 400-500 billion rupiah to fund its expansion project.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 INVESTOR DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - TRUBA ALAM EYES 550 BILLION RUPIAH FROM IPO  \par \par \uc2 An Indonesian engineering company, PT Truba Alam Manunggal Engineering Tbk, is aiming to raise 550 billion rupiah ($59.79 million) from an initial public offering this month.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 ($1=9,198 rupiah)  \par \par \uc2 PRESS-INDONESIA-BUSINESS|LANGEN|IF|G|RBN|REVU|ABN|E|RNP|DNP|PGE  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061006e2a600011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
