\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia: USD Likely Below IDR9,000 By End '06  \b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2006\par 08:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar may drop below IDR9,000 by the end of 2006, Bank Indonesia's deputy governor said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe there is room in that direction, as our exports have been good enough, and we hope to control inflation," Aslim Tadjuddin told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin said inflation would likely remain in check throughout August. While he didn't specify a projection for inflation figure, he indicated it would likely be near July's level.  \par \par \uc2 "Last month, inflation was 0.45% (on month), and hopefully we can control inflation this month also," he said. [ 25-08-06 0637GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin's comments suggest that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be rethinking its traditional de facto policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at perceived "psychologically important" levels in order to maintain the country's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia's policy is to allow the market to determine the rupiah's movements but hedges that position by reserving the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent "volatility" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "Even though in the last few days (the rupiah) has weakened, that is a temporary shift in line with the movements of global and regional (\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "So I predict that the rupiah will continue to trend upwards from its current position."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at IDR9,144 at 0712 GMT, up from an intraday low of IDR9,123.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin's stance is likely to draw fire from Vice President Jusuf Kalla, who has repeatedly expressed his preference for the dollar to trade around IDR9,500 to help boost exports.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's successful efforts to control inflation had created "substantial room" for future cuts in the benchmark Bank Indonesia one-month rate.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia cut its benchmark rate by 50 basis points to 11.75% earlier this month, the third and steepest such decline since monetary policy easing began in May.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the benchmark Bank Indonesia rate to fall to around 11% by the end of this year, in tandem with an expected decline in on-year inflation to around 8% in the same period. Indonesia's on-year inflation in July was 15.15%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia's Board of Governors will decide next on possible benchmark rate movements at a monthly meeting on Sept. 5.  \par \par \uc2 -By Reuben Carder; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; reuben.carder@dowjones.com [ 25-08-06 0749GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060825e28p0008r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
