\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Rupiah Ends Down; Tight Liquidity Limits Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2006\par 11:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed lower Friday as rising oil prices dragged most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 But tight rupiah supply in the interbank money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the local unit claw back some of the losses, dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 'The rupiah was not spared by the weakness of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,180, up from its close Thursday at IDR9,103, after rising to an intraday high of IDR9,253 earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said a huge corporate tax payment due Friday drained rupiah liquidity from the market, which in turn pushed the overnight interbank rupiah lending rate to 15% from 8%. The rising interbank overnight rate eventually sparked players to trim their dollar-long positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  admitted it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Friday to help the rupiah, and promised more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the dollar to be stable around IDR9,200, Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin told reporters Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar still looks well-bid Monday on uncertainties over oil prices globally. They expect the greenback to trade between IDR9,125 and IDR9,250 Monday. -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Senta