\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Higher as stocks, Fed, lift sentiment  \b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2006\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Friday, bouncing back from this week's multi-month lows thanks to a broad rebound in equities, upbeat U.S. economic data and a rise in the yuan to a post-revaluation high against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said remarks on inflation from Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on Thursday appeared less hawkish than comments made a week ago, helping trigger stock market gains.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke said the Fed's inflation-fighting credibility had limited the degree to which lofty energy costs have bled into other prices paid by American consumers.  \par \par \uc2 Data on Thursday showing solid U.S. regional manufacturing activity also eased concerns about a slowdown in growth, helping boost sentiment in fragile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 "What we're seeing is anxiety about the U.S. is diminishing for now and the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should strengthen," said Tim Condon, head of research at ING in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> rose as much as 0.6 percent to 953.9 per dollar as local shares notched up their biggest one-day percentage gain in more than 1-\u189\'00\'BD years.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar, which hit a 5-month low at about 32.75 per dollar on Wednesday, hit a one-week peak at 32.40, while the Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose as high as 1.5862 -- rebounding almost one percent from a low of 1.5999 per dollar hit this week.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> also touched a one-week high at 52.98 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "We are going into a consolidation phase and a dollar-selling trend is unlikely to start so soon as the market continues to focus on inflation and imbalances in the global economy," said Philip Wee, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS Bank in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 The rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aided by the yuan <CNY=CFXS>, which hit 7.9970 per dollar -- the highest level since its revaluation in July last year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say a pick up in yuan gains this week suggest China is using the exchange rate in its battle to slow the economy.  \par \par \uc2 RUPIAH, RINGGIT FIRM  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> firmed as much as 1 percent to 9,289 per dollar, the highest level in more than a week and comfortably stronger than Wednesday's 5-month low at 9,560.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there had been no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupiah after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "in the market" to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A trader said there had been signals from foreign banks of renewed investor interest in Indonesian assets such as bonds.  \par \par \uc2 "The yields are just too attractive," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on 8-year government bonds soared to 13 percent at an auction on Tuesday, compared with 11.95 percent at a similar sale in April. Indonesian bond yields are among Asia's highest.  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> rose to its strongest in more than a week at 3.6361 per dollar, up more than 1.5 percent from this week's 2-\u189\'00\'BD month trough at 3.6945.  \par \par \uc2 Sharp moves in the ringgit this week suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is further easing its tight grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pretty much accepted the ringgit is going to be more volatile if you open it up, especially at this juncture when overseas markets and all assets types are seeing higher volatility," said a dealer in Kuala Lumpur. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0804 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.72         114.92       +0.17\par  Sing dlr        1.5880         1.5910       +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr      32.476         32.541       +0.20\par  Korean won      955.40         959.50       +0.43\par  Baht             38.31          38.38       +0.18\par  Peso             53.11          53.13       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9323.00        9385.00       +0.67\par  Rupee            45.92          45.98       +0.13\par  Ringgit         3.6470         3.6540       +0.19\par  Yuan            7.9987         7.9997       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.72         117.96       +2.82\par  Sing dlr        1.5880         1.6625       +4.69\par  Taiwan dlr      32.476         32.850       +1.15\par  Korean won      955.40        1011.60       +5.88\par  Baht             38.31          41.11       +7.31\par  Peso             53.11          53.09       -0.04\par  Rupiah         9323.00        9835.00       +5.49\par  Rupee            45.92          45.04       -1.92\par  Ringgit         3.6470         3.7790       +3.62\par  Yuan            7.9987         8.0702       +0.89\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060619e26g0005b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shp