\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Higher On Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Rebound  \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2006\par 12:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Thursday on the back of a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebound against the U.S. dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah gained against the greenback due to large-scale dollar sales in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by offshore investors including Singapore-based foreign investment banks, according to a dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We also saw some dollar selling by state banks, likely on behalf of Bank Indonesia," the dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,385 compared to IDR9,478 on Wednesday. That reflects a strengthening in the rupiah since the dollar's more-than-six-month high Tuesday of IDR9,505 powered by foreign investors' concerns about a widely anticipated U.S. Federal Reserve Rate hike on June 29.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the rupiah comes as no surprise to the market.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah told reporters Thursday that his staff was closely monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the rupiah from any serious volatility against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "We are in the market," Abdullah said.  \par \par \uc2 "We do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...in times when the rupiah is stronger and when the rupiah weakens."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers indicated that such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue to be necessary in the days ahead to counter the impact of jittery foreign investors warily awaiting the Fed decision later this month.  \par \par \uc2 "If nothing happens in New York tonight, the dollar should remain around the IDR9,350 level on Friday," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "But if something bad happens in New York time tonight, we will easily hit IDR9,500 (tomorrow)," he added.  \par \par \uc2 -By Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by David Bottomley [ 15-06-06 1037GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060615e26f000ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
