\par\par \b \uc2 PRECIOUS METAL UPDATE: Pres Role Sought In Freeport Talks  \b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2006\par 08:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   TOP STORIES: \par  \par INDONESIA PRESS: President's Role Sought In Freeport Talks   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The renegotiation of PT Freeport Indonesia's contract to operate the giant Grasberg copper and gold mine in Papua province requires presidential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Investor Daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reported Wednesday, citing statements from three non-governmental organizations.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: Metals Rebound Flows Through To Asian Markets   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--A commodity-wide rebound in European and North American trade overnight flowed through to Asian markets Wednesday with several metal futures contracts in the region hitting their daily upper limits.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Gold Investment Demand Soars In Volatile 1Q 2006 -Council   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Persistent interest from differing groups of institutional investors drove the gold price to new highs in the first quarter of 2006 while investment instruments like the gold exchange-traded fund, or ETF, saw its largest quarterly increase, the World Gold Council reported in its quarterly review released Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par After 1Q Drop, Gold Jewelry Demand Picks Up In 2Q -Council   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Demand for gold jewelry is experiencing a slight recovery so far in the second quarter of 2006 after dropping by 22% in the first quarter, said George Milling-Stanley, manager of market analysis at World Gold Council.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Speculative, Physical Buying Underpin Comex Gold, Silver   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Broad-based buying - including both physical interest and speculative accounts - has enabled gold and silver futures to rise sharply so far Tuesday, traders and analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: Financial Jitters Offer Gold N/T Pain, L/T Gain   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Global financial uncertainties have cast a shadow over gold and other commodities, but as a safe haven asset, the metal's long-term outlook remains bright, analysts said Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    STORIES OF INTEREST: \par  \par Peru's April Exports Up 35% On Yr At $1.68 Bln - Govt   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Improved sales of gold, copper and zinc helped lift Peru's exports to $1.68 billion in April, 35% higher than in the same month a year earlier, government agency Prompex said Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB Gold Reserves -EUR26M, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  +EUR300M In Wk To May 19   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Eurosystem's reserves of gold and gold receivables decreased EUR26 million to EUR179.547 billion in the week ended May 19, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PNG's Highlands Suffers 2nd Setback At Gold Mine   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Papua New Guinea-based Highlands Pacific Ltd. (HIG.AU) said Tuesday its company-making Kainantu gold mine has suffered the second shutdown since Prime Minister Michael Somare opened the mine in March.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Jubilee Platinum Reports Excellent Tjate Drill Results   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Jubilee Platinum Tuesday announced excellent results for its borehole DT6 on the Dsjate farm in the Bushveld Complex of South Africa.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China To Set Up Institute To Manage Gold Reserves -Report   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will set up a reserves-management center in Shanghai to oversee its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve investments in gold, Shanghai Securities News reported Tuesday, citing an unnamed source familiar with the situation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    MARKETS: \par  \par NY Precious Metals Review: Sharp Gains As Crude Bounces   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The entire precious metals complex rose sharply Tuesday as speculative buying returned after a recent correction lower, aided by a bounce in crude oil, traders and analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Spot Gold Ends Up, Tracks Global Rise   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Spot gold traded on the Shanghai Gold Exchange closed a tad higher Tuesday after an overnight recovery in international spot gold.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By James Attwood, Dow Jones Newswires; 612-8235-2957; james.attwood@dowjones.com [ 05-24-06 0235ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 61069 82203  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020060524e25o0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
