\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends 5% Dn At 2-Mo Low On Fund Outflows  \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2006\par 11:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The rupiah fell nearly 5% Monday to end at a two-month low against the dollar as hedge funds exited Indonesia as part of their risk aversion strategy on emerging markets, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,160, up from its close Friday at IDR8,735. Monday's close is the greenback's highest closing level since March 14, when it ended at 9,165.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar outflows came mostly from the stock market, which fell 6.3% Monday, the largest single drop ever.  \par \par \uc2 Inflows of speculative funds seeking high yields had been cited as the main force that brought the rupiah to its four-year high recently.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Burhanduddin Abdullah said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday to curb the dollar's rise, and vowed to do it again to bring the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its "appropriate level" of IDR8,750.  \par \par \uc2 He said that the rupiah fell as hedge funds exited emerging markets after some of them suffered losses in Brazil and Turkey recently.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank Indonesia had failed to contained the dollar's rise as the amount of dollars it sold in the market was likely marginal.  \par \par \uc2 "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to curb the dollar's rise," a dealer with a foreign bank said. "Given the speed of the dollar's rise today, IDR9,500 doesn't seem to be very far away."  \par \par \uc2 Still, Finance Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati told parliament Monday that the dollar will likely remain below IDR9,000 until the end of the year. Mulyani didn't give any reason.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that news of Indonesia's slowing economic growth in the first quarter was well expected, but added to the dampened sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Statistics Agency said that Southeast Asia's largest economy expanded 4.59% on year in the first quarter, slowing from 4.90% on year in the fourth quarter of 2005. It is a tad lower than the average forecast of economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires of 4.61%.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to test IDR9,200 upside resistance Tuesday, with IDR8,990 seen as solid support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 If IDR9,200 is broken, dealers expect the dollar to scale higher toward IDR9,400, Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 15-05-06 0948GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060515e25f000nd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
