\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower As State Banks Buy Dollars  \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2006\par 11:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly lower Thursday on dollar bids from state banks, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR8,735, up from its previous close of IDR8,726.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said state banks bought the greenback at levels between IDR8,720 and IDR8,730, likely on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I think Bank Indonesia was behind the state banks," a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia is suspected of buying the dollar recently to slow its slide against the local unit. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials usually decline to comment on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the authority's top officials have said the bank doesn't want a volatile market.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar's rebound against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following the U.S. Federal Reserve's move to hike its key rate by 25 basis points Wednesday, sparked dollar buying when trading started.  \par \par \uc2 But foreign banks mostly took the dollar's rise as an opportunity to sell it at higher levels, spurred by their positive sentiment toward Indonesia, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,720 and IDR8,740 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 11-05-06 0932GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060511e25b000nq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pic