\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesian Rupiah Ends Higher On Offshore Invest Inflows  \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 11:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended at a more-than-15-month high Tuesday, powered by offshore investors buying into Indonesia's equities market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,114, down from Monday's close of IDR9,140 and marking the lowest end-of-day result for the U.S. unit since the IDR9,097 level reached on Dec. 7, 2004.  \par \par \uc2 'Offshore inflows for equities and other offshore investment money just keeps coming into the country,' a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 'I think the trend is still pretty bullish for the rupiah.'  \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Stock Exchange Composite Index edged down 0.2% Tuesday, but that followed three days of gains that ended with a 1.8% rise Monday to a record close of 1330.113 points.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have been piling into Indonesia's equities markets due to increasingly upbeat sentiment about the country's economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 The government has targeted economic growth of 6.2% in 2006, which would outpace the 5.6% increase in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 High expectations that President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono's economic cabinet team will make significant progress this year in reducing regulatory and bureaucratic obstacles to investment growth are fueling investor sentiment, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the greenback will strengthen against the rupiah in the days ahead as local corporates make routine end-month dollar purchases to service foreign debt obligations.  \par \par \uc2 But subtle \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-owned banks will likely keep the greenback from falling below the IDR9,000 level this week, dealers say.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia officials routinely express their support for market forces determining the value of the rupiah against the dollar, but hedge those comments by adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to prevent potentially disruptive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.  \par \par \uc2 'We'll probably see Bank Indonesia selling dollars through state banks to smooth out the recent rise,' a dealer said, without elaborating.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the greenback will trade in a IDR9,090 to IDR9,115 band Wednesday. -By Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060321e23l007es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
