\par\par \b \uc2 Traders:USD Falls Below IDR9,400; 1st Time Since Mar 23  \b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2006\par 02:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)-The U.S. dollar fell below the IDR9,400 mark in early trading Thursday for the first time since March 23, 2005, traders told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was being taken at IDR9,395 at 0155 GMT traders said, the lowest point since it fell to IDR9,378 in intraday trading March 23 before rebounding above the IDR9,400 mark the following day.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say the rupiah's strength is underpinned by a combination of strong offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows into Indonesia's stock market and a surge in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. [ 12-01-06 0210GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Stock Exchange Composite Index ended up 1.3%, or 16.229 points, at a new closing high of 1261.283 Wednesday, surpassing the previous record of 1245.054 Monday. Indonesia was closed Tuesday for a holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said expectations of a steady interest-rate environment after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its benchmark Bank Indonesia rate unchanged Monday at 12.75% triggered buying, offsetting sporadic profit-taking by local retail funds.  \par \par \uc2 The index is likely to rise higher Thursday on the rupiah's surge against the dollar and gains in other Asian equities markets, dealers said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupiah's rise is highly unlikely, dealers and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia perceives the rupiah's strength as a useful tool in curbing inflation, which hit 17.11% in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin said Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserved its right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but insisted that "we leave to the market" the value of the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no need for Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as (the dollar slide) is due to market forces," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta said.  \par \par \uc2 That view was echoed by the secretary of the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dealer Association, Panji Irawan.  \par \par \uc2 "We have seen the dollar at IDR8,300, and at that level our exports were still competitive," Panji said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point would likely be fruitless, BNP Paribas senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Thio Chin Loo said. "Most people agree there's no point in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...it would be like trying to catch a falling knife or fighting against a huge flock of birds flying the same way."  \par \par \uc2 A "feel-good factor" toward Asian markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , combined with concerns about U.S. macroeconomic data and signals that the U.S. Federal Reserve is about to stop hiking rates, are underpinning the dollar's slide, Thio said.  \par \par \uc2 "This is still a dollar story ... people are jumping on the (dollar sale) bandwagon and momentum is strong," Thio said.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana and Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 12-01-06 0327GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060112e21c00020\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph1